NHS medics are dying and dr. alpha sadhu  is one the nigerian-born retired medical  director spent his whole career in the  NHS and was also a devoted grandfather  he was working with elderly patients  just one day a week with no protective  equipment yet still managed to catch the  virus his condition deteriorated on  Sunday after two weeks of staying at  home but he resisted using up stretched  NHS resources we said goodbye to him not  knowing that that would be the last time  we'd seen and after that from Sunday  evening to Tuesday morning he just  deteriorated body shut down organ  failure I've never seen anything you  know I'm both my parents and doctors I'm  quite experienced or quite experienced  with different diseases and viruses  they're out there but I've never seen  anything like this 7 unions have called  the lack of PPE a crisis within a crisis  saying medics are being exposed to  unreasonable and unnecessary risk by the  failure to provide adequate PPE several  doctors have told us about their worries  unlike a lot of the military rhetoric  which is happening right now we are not  soldiers that are trained for war we are  ordinary human beings who have families  who have terrified for our safety and we  are terrified for their safety because  the reality is that we could be bringing  this virus home to the people that we  love most  many health workers are buying  protective equipment themselves or  getting donations amid claims that  complaints directly to the media are met  with threats and pressure to stop we've  been hearing from frontline doctors in  their droves who have concerns about  personal protective equipment about the  lack of testing of frontline staff and  as they've raised these concerns locally  they've essentially been gagged by  either managers or senior managers  within their organizations they've been  told that their social media for example  is being monitored and that if they were  to raise concerns that in some cases  their jobs and positions will become  untenable for dr. Saudis family the loss  is immeasurable and his son Danny warned  others to take the virus seriously I  remember when Boris Johnson said on the  news a few weeks ago he said you know  you prepared to lose loved ones and at  the time when he said I got really angry  I just thought you know this is not a  movie why are you saying this you know  you're overdramatizing this and I know  understand what he means I've learned  the hard way people really need to take  this seriously this is this isn't a joke  his father is viewed as a hero by many  one of an increasing number but behind  all these statistics are real people  real lives lost leaving real families  behind Alex Crawford Sky News North  London
 

